00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:36,090
to changing the budgeting process in your research department.

276
00:21:36,090 --> 00:21:39,690
You better keep that for a head in front of you

277
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:42,430
till you have finished doing it

278
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:46,030
as a constant reminder that you have committed yourself

279
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:50,070
to a major change that requires a lot of work.

280
00:21:50,790 --> 00:22:14,520
If not so, I don't think that's a function of the relationship.

281
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:17,220
I think that's a function of your own native intelligence.

282
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:20,300
It's just stupid to underrate the boss.

283
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,960
Yet very bright young people do it all the time.

284
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:29,140
Is there a rating on the boss?

285
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,340
Very little, as a rule,

286
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:35,640
because you risk nothing by overrating him.

287
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:39,700
And if it turns out you haven't overrated him at all,

288
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:42,160
well, then you have an ally, then you have a support.

289
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:46,880
The worst that can happen is that you're too shrewd.

290
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:52,080
If you systematically lose because you overestimate the boss,

291
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:57,420
get out, because that means you're working under an incompetent boss.

292
00:22:57,420 --> 00:23:03,470
One of the things to learn about managing anything is when to abandon.

293
00:23:03,750 --> 00:23:08,290
This is also a chapter heading in managing the boss.

294
00:23:08,630 --> 00:23:10,630
When do you abandon a boss?

295
00:23:11,250 --> 00:23:18,030
There is still no better prescription for success than to have a boss who is going

296
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:28,090
and no more certain prescription for frustration and failure than to work for an incumbent.

297
00:23:28,090 --> 00:23:34,210
If you overreach the boss in the sense that the things that are right,

298
00:23:35,300 --> 00:23:41,570
he's just unwilling, unable, incapable of grasping and of doing,

299
00:23:41,730 --> 00:23:43,450
you have an incompetent boss.

300
00:23:44,090 --> 00:23:48,770
And then that is one of the few cases where I would always counsel

301
00:23:48,770 --> 00:23:55,160
in favor of exchange, a transfer, change in jobs.

302
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:59,850
And the other one is a corrupt boss.

303
00:23:59,850 --> 00:24:04,400
And I don't mean one who dips his hands into the till.

304
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:05,960
That's one form of corruption.

305
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:08,020
But the most serious form of corruption

306
00:24:08,020 --> 00:24:12,720
is one who has values, standards, that

307
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:16,680
are ethically and morally unacceptable to you,

308
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:19,280
that just demean you.

309
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:25,670
One does not ask because one will become corrupt oneself.

310
00:24:25,670 --> 00:24:28,690
One will become contemptuous of oneself.

311
00:24:28,690 --> 00:24:31,170
One will begin to lose oneself.

312
00:24:31,170 --> 00:24:35,930
So if you work for an incompetent or for a corrupt boss, get out.

313
00:24:37,170 --> 00:24:41,590
Those are the two cases where I think one says,

314
00:24:41,590 --> 00:24:46,350
all right, I like the company, but it isn't going to work out.

315
00:24:47,220 --> 00:24:49,500
One abandons. One looks for something else.

316
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:53,560
If you have three children going to college

317
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:56,210
and you have to pay a lot of alimony,

318
00:24:57,490 --> 00:25:01,920
well, maybe you are a little reluctant to take that risk.

319
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:17,480
But if you at all can look elsewhere, in the company or outside, rather than keep on for the boss, one should abandon.

320
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:26,020
What if the boss...

321
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:38,850
Yes. And in fact, if the boss is a paragon, it's easy to stay too long because it's easy to become an assistant to rather than your own man.

322
00:25:38,850 --> 00:25:50,360
There's a great deal of fear, less today than there was 10 years ago, about the organization man whom the organization views as having to become the servant.

323
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:58,800
Never been enough emphasis on the opposite, that it is your job to look upon the organization as your tool.

324
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:07,800
And one looks at a job with two questions, what can I contribute and what can it contribute to me?

325
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:12,960
what has it done for me lately and what is it likely to do for me in the future.

326
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:19,920
If you find yourself in a position in which you have gotten as much out of the job,

327
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:24,680
out of the boss, out of the work, as it will ever give you,

328
00:26:24,780 --> 00:26:27,300
and you are still below late middle age,

329
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:31,480
you are still concerned with where am I going to go,

330
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:35,920
who am I going to be, what opportunities do I have,

331
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:38,200
Then one moves out.

332
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:46,580
Then one says, all right, I've gotten everything out of this company, this work, this boss.

333
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:55,950
It's likely to give me, and I've given as much as I'm likely to give, and now it's time for me to move on.

334
00:26:56,470 --> 00:27:05,820
One doesn't do it too often, and one doesn't rush, but one keeps in mind that there is a time limit.

335
00:27:05,820 --> 00:27:09,800
One moves out because of success as much as failure.

336
00:27:10,620 --> 00:27:41,980
Yes, in today's society, everyone has a boss, even the company president and the chief executive officer is accountable to a board, to stockholders, today very heavily to a lot of outside regulatory and other agencies, just as the hospital administrator is accountable to his board and to the community.

337
00:27:41,980 --> 00:27:48,420
and even the President of the United States, as we found out a few years ago,

338
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:52,480
can be held accountable to the voters and to the Congress.

339
00:27:53,480 --> 00:28:01,350
You don't have to like and to admire your boss, nor do you have to hate him.

340
00:28:01,350 --> 00:28:07,130
You do, however, have to manage him so that he becomes your resource

341
00:28:07,130 --> 00:28:10,580
for achievement, for accomplishment.

342
00:28:10,580 --> 00:28:16,180
and let's be candid about it for personal success as well.

343
