00:28:51,190 --> 00:28:56,190
because I think every craftsman has a specific toolkit

345
00:28:56,190 --> 00:29:01,360
and the manager is a craftsman or should be a craftsman.

346
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:07,680
And the tools in his toolkit are very different from those of the carpenter,

347
00:29:07,780 --> 00:29:08,600
but they are tools.

348
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:17,970
There is first, I think, the meeting. Managers need to know how to use the meeting as a tool.

349
00:29:19,660 --> 00:29:27,780
There is a report that distinct managerial affliction, and how do you make a report effective,

350
00:29:28,220 --> 00:29:37,620
which means, above all, how do you make reasonably certain that it will be read and understood and acted upon.

351
00:29:37,620 --> 00:29:53,180
There is the control of assignments, the control of what the people who work in a manager's group are supposed to be working on.

352
00:29:54,180 --> 00:29:59,700
There is the appraisal of performance and the appraisal of the performer.

353
00:30:00,340 --> 00:30:02,020
There are two different things, I believe.

354
00:30:02,880 --> 00:30:04,880
There is a development of people.

355
00:30:06,060 --> 00:30:11,640
And finally, there is a need to learn how to abandon yesterday.

356
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:21,390
There is a great deal of emphasis and deserved emphasis on starting anew, on innovation,

357
00:30:21,390 --> 00:30:32,390
on creativity, but one cannot innovate unless one abandons the old, and one cannot be creative

358
00:30:32,390 --> 00:30:39,770
if one keeps on doing the routine, so one has to learn how to organize abandonment.

